     This setting should **not** be used when running multiple bots on the same account. Please look at [Available Capital to the bot](#assign-available-capital) instead.
 
+#### Underlying currency exposure limit
+
+If several of your traded pairs are priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency (for example a handful of pairs settled in BTC, or several coins quoted in the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit multiple of your open trades at once - even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_underlying_currency_exposure` lets you cap the share of your tradable capital that may be committed at the same time to open trades sharing the same underlying (settlement, or - for spot - quote) currency. It defaults to `1` (100%), which applies no additional restriction beyond the existing sizing limits.
+
+For example, setting `"max_underlying_currency_exposure": 0.3` ensures that no more than 30% of your tradable capital is ever tied up at once in trades settled in the same currency, regardless of how many separate pairs contribute to that exposure.
+
+When opening (or adding to) a trade would push the combined exposure of its underlying currency above the configured limit, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit - the same way freqtrade already reduces the stake amount when it exceeds other limits (e.g. exchange or balance limits). If no stake is left, the trade is skipped. This applies identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
 !!! Warning
     The `tradable_balance_ratio` setting applies to the current balance (free balance + tied up in trades). Therefore, assuming the starting balance of 1000, a configuration with `tradable_balance_ratio=0.99` will not guarantee that 10 currency units will always remain available on the exchange. For example, the free amount may reduce to 5 units if the total balance is reduced to 500 (either by a losing streak or by withdrawing balance).
 
